-- PREPENDED, not appended: sql.js stops at its first throw, so the §GEOREF block must land before
-- anything below it can fail. Everything after the marked line predates this block, unchanged.
--
-- NOTHING HERE IS COMPUTED OR ESTIMATED. Values are what DAGCompiler/python/extractIFCtoDB.py
-- `extract_georef` (BIMCompiler#117) returns on the source below — the function was RUN,
-- ifcopenshell 0.8.4, 2026-09-19, and reproduced independently by a second SPF reader.
--
-- SOURCE: internal/UNMERGED/LTU_AHouse_ARC.ifc
-- PROVENANCE: GUID match, not filename — this DB's elements_meta guids carry the
--   T0_LTU_AHouse_ prefix and hit the LTU_AHouse_*.ifc set.
--
-- ⚠ THE SOURCES DISAGREE, AND THE STANDING RULING SETTLES IT. Of the nine discipline files,
-- seven (AIR, COOL, DUCT, HEAT, PLB, SAN, VOID) carry no lat/long at all, and the two that do
-- disagree by about 20 km:
--     ARC   59.33333333 / 18.05000000   (this file — the architectural master)
--     STR   59.28110000 / 17.80680000
-- RULING, red1, 2026-09-18, recorded on Hospital_extracted.db.sql and applied here: ARC is the
-- AUTHORITATIVE SOURCE OF RECORD; STR/MEP/MECH are the errors. That is a rule about which file
-- speaks for the project, not about which number looks more surveyed — so "ARC's value is a round
-- 59 deg 20' / 18 deg 03' and STR's is not" is NOT a reason to reopen it. Reading precision as
-- authority is exactly the closest-to-plausible heuristic the Hospital patch forbids.
--
-- Corroborating, and a fact rather than a judgement: LTU_AHouse_STR.ifc is ALSO one of the four
-- files in this fleet whose TrueNorth is malformed — IFCDIRECTION((2.0, 6.123e-17, 1.0)), a
-- three-component direction with z=1.0 that the extractor REFUSES by name
-- (`malformed_truenorth_ignored`, extractIFCtoDB.py). The file this ruling sets aside is the same
-- file the code already refuses to take a bearing from.
--
-- true_north_angle 0.000000 here is a REAL authored zero from ARC (`ifc_truenorth`), not the old
-- stub — that is why the source key exists, and it must not be tidied to `default_zero`.
--
-- Applying this twice changes nothing (INSERT OR REPLACE on a PRIMARY KEY).
-- ============================================================================================
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS project_metadata (key TEXT PRIMARY KEY, value TEXT);
